{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A0",
  "unit": 1,
  "title": "Hello",
  "description": "Greet someone, and be polite about it.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Greeting someone in Spanish is mostly a matter of picking the right phrase for the time of day. Hola works at any hour, and the rest are built around buenos and buenas.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The three good ones",
        "body": "Buenos días is for the morning, buenas tardes for the afternoon, and buenas noches for the evening. The adjective agrees: buenos and buenas. The noun that goes with them is singular, and that is what makes them look odd: literally good days, good afternoon and good evenings.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Buenos días, señora.",
            "en": "Good morning, madam."
          },
          {
            "es": "Buenas tardes, ¿cómo está?",
            "en": "Good afternoon, how are you?"
          },
          {
            "es": "Buenas noches, hasta mañana.",
            "en": "Good evening, see you tomorrow."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Saying hello and goodbye",
        "body": "Hola works at any time of day, and it is the safest greeting. Adiós is a goodbye for leaving or ending a conversation. Hasta luego is see you later, and it works for leaving. Adiós carries a slight formality that hasta luego does not.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Hola, me llamo Ana.",
            "en": "Hello, my name is Ana."
          },
          {
            "es": "Adiós, hasta mañana.",
            "en": "Goodbye, see you tomorrow."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Being polite",
        "body": "Gracias is thank you, and it never changes. De nada is the answer, and it means literally it is nothing. Por favor goes before the thing you are asking for: un café, por favor. Yes is sí, with an accent, and no is no.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Gracias por tu ayuda.",
            "en": "Thank you for your help."
          },
          {
            "es": "Un café con leche, por favor.",
            "en": "A coffee with milk, please."
          },
          {
            "es": "De nada.",
            "en": "You are welcome."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
